{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 25, :comments ["<b>And there shall be eight planks.</b> These are the ones stated above: 'You shall make six planks, and two planks you shall make for the corners' — so there are eight planks on the western side. So it is taught in the Mishnah, in the tractate of the arrangement of the planks in the work of the Tabernacle: He would make the sockets hollow, and he would cut away the plank from below — a quarter from here and a quarter from here, and the cut would be half its thickness in the middle. And he would make for it two tenons like two dowels — and it seems to me the reading is 'like two חֲוָקִין,' like two rungs of a ladder set apart one from the other — and smooth to enter into the hollow of the socket, like a rung that enters into the hole of a ladder's upright. And that is the sense of מְשֻׁלָּבוֹת — made like a rung — and he inserts them into two sockets, as it says: 'שְׁנֵי אֲדָנִים שְׁנֵי אֲדָנִים' — 'two sockets, two sockets.' And he would cut away the plank from above — a finger-breadth from here and a finger-breadth from here, and insert them into a single ring of gold so they would not separate one from the other, as it says: 'וְיִהְיוּ תֹאֲמִים מִלְּמַטָּה' — 'and they shall be joined beneath,' and so on. That is the Mishnah, and its explanation I set forth above, in the order of the verses."], :book :exodus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 26, :notes {0 "Rashi distinguishes between the reading 'חֲמוּקִין' ('curved/bent') and the reading he prefers, 'חֲוָקִין', which he glosses as ladder-rungs; both are preserved in the translation."}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:54:53.058048080Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}